{"name":"Vanderbilt Beach","hex":"#d8cbb3","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vanderbilt Beach, Florida","blocks":[{"text":"Vanderbilt Beach is an unincorporated community in Collier County, Florida, United States. It is located north of the Pelican Bay census-designated place and west of Naples Park, along the Gulf of Mexico. Vanderbilt Beach is 9 miles (14 km) north of the center of Naples. Vanderbilt Beach shares the ZIP code 34108 with Naples Park and North Naples."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanderbilt_Beach%2C_Florida","wikidata":"Q7914434"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg/500px-Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg/1280px-Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0d/Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg/500px-Vanderbilt_Beach.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vanderbilt Beach north of Naples, Florida","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVanderbilt_Beach.jpeg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/1280px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg/500px-Lago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALago_di_Lavarone_190820_03.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/1280px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg/500px-Man_o%27war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMan_o'war_cove_near_lulworth_dorset_arp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/Beach_zones.png/500px-Beach_zones.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A berm is a nearly horizontal portion that stays dry except during extremely high tides and storms. The swash zone is alternately covered and exposed by wave run-up. The beach face is the sloping section below the berm that is exposed to the swash of the waves. The wrack line (not shown here) is the highest reach of the daily tide where organic and inorganic debris is deposited by wave action. May have sand dunes.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABeach_zones.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Summer_versus_winter_beach.png/500px-Summer_versus_winter_beach.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The differences between summer and winter on beaches in areas where the winter conditions are rougher and waves have a shorter wavelength but higher energy. In winter, sand from the beach is stored offshore.[2]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASummer_versus_winter_beach.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/500px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/1280px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg/500px-Scala_dei_Turchi_Sand_062313.jpg?utm_source=e